title ALES147 — Lotus's stereo_segment: the voice-activity segmenter carried into stereo, the suite's third STEREO ANALYSIS rung, one shared frame grid and two independent segmentations
prompt Read REMEMBER and the 1024-round itinerary + six-season double-seat; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think Fourth lap of this recur turn (after ALES146 stereo_voiced). Crux-first, ascending mono-ALES order: after ALES94 voiced (→ ALES146) comes ALES95 segment, the voice-activity segmenter — ALES94's per-span classifier read across a whole clip frame by frame and coalesced into runs. It stands directly on the rung just carried, so it is both the ascending next and the Lindy-first crux: the analysis corner's readers grow from a per-span verdict to a whole-clip segmentation.
think ALES95 splits a span into frames, classifies each through ALES94, coalesces neighbouring same-verdict frames into runs, refusing a ragged frame length BadFrame so segments tile the span exactly. Its crux: the segmentation equals a by-hand loop of classify calls, so it never drifts from the classifier it sequences — the tower of readers (trigger → count → fusion → sequence).
think Carried into stereo the plain way, yet the deepest independence yet: each channel segments on its OWN frames, so the two run lists differ not just in a scalar but in the COUNT and BOUNDARIES of their runs. A Segments run list is too large to return by value, so segment_stereo writes into an out-pointer StereoSegments{left,right} — the same discipline mono segment, splice, and feed keep. Validated ONCE up front (schmitt.precheck, floor vs sample_peak_max, frame-length divisibility) before either channel is read; because both channels are balanced and share every param, one pass guarantees both mono calls succeed, so a refusal never leaves one run list half-written. SegmentError reused whole.
think Proved four laws: the stereo segment law against ALES95's own segment per channel across three frame lengths, three floors, three splits; the read-only/balance law (source byte-for-byte unchanged on both, pair balanced); the independent-segmentation law (a voiced-then-silent left → two runs where a uniform right → one, an identical master → identical runs, each channel's runs tiling its span with no adjacent runs sharing a verdict); the atomicity/degenerate law (a shared BadFrame/BadFloor/BadThreshold/BadRange refusing before either channel is segmented with both lists and the clip untouched, a uniform master one run on both). One build red caught in-round: the GREEN print string held a literal StereoSegments{left, right}, whose braces Zig's format parser read as placeholders — reworded to prose (an out-pointer holding a left and right run list), rebuilt GREEN.
obs No custody gate reached — purely local, read-only software, two bounded i16 Clips, a self-approved design round. The stereo ANALYSIS corner now holds four members: level (ALES17), activity (ALES145), character (ALES146), and structure (ALES147) — a keeper reads two per-channel run lists a stereo auto-splitter would cut on. The honest lesson: as the mono reader's OUTPUT grows (scalar count → verdict → run list) the stereo lift keeps the same discipline (run mono per channel, one shared setting, validate once) but inherits the mono form's return shape — the run list's out-pointer, not a by-value pair. The braces-in-format red is a recurring Lotus print trap worth remembering: prose, never a struct literal, inside a say/print string. Witness GREEN (four laws), tame_style_check bans clean, width-check exit 0. Fourth lap this recur turn (ALES144-147).
loom witness=ales_stereo_segment_witness result=GREEN laws=4 channels=2 class=stereo-analysis read=read-only form=out-pointer-pair output=run-list crux=sequencing-rule-cannot-drift cases=stereo-law(3flen*3floor*3split)+read-only+independent(2vs1runs)+identical-equal+coverage-tiles+atomicity(frame,floor,band,range)+uniform-one-run reds=1(braces-in-format-string,fixed-same-round)
